{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And afterward.</b> After Aaron performed the signs, both of them came to Pharaoh, and both of them said to him that HaShem had promised them, \"I will be with your mouth and with his mouth\" (above, Exodus 4:15)." "<b>And they said: Thus says HaShem.</b> And this name Pharaoh had not heard; therefore he mentioned \"the Elohim of Israel,\" and the meaning is the people of Israel, and not Jacob alone." "<b>And they shall hold a festival to Me in the wilderness.</b> To sacrifice sacrifices, as in \"bind the festival with boughs\" (Psalms 118:27), \"the festivals are recounted\" (Isaiah 29:1)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:47.042600340Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}